\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The ladder at $\ensuremath  {K^{\star }}$, one panel per rival set, 3 seeds; every panel title prints the rivals' fit pool and optimiser steps.} Distinct valid novel tuples per corner against $n$: the store beside (a)~the read-path-matched rivals fitted on the 32,256-row combination-split pool for 5,040 steps, (b)~the data-matched MLP fitted for 2,560 steps on the same 32,768 rows of each rung's pool as the store's content, and (c)~the four data-matched rivals fitted on each rung's own 131,072-row pool, the store's exact rows, at 20,480 steps, or at 204,800 where the 20,480-step fit had not converged (filled dots), with the table floor in every panel (Table~\ref {tab:ladder}). Open markers are the seeds; the line is their mean. The store's margin over the strongest rival is smallest against (c) on every rung, and the store stays above every drawn rival on every rung and seed. For $n\ge 3$ the rungs probe the identical 120 corners, so the horizontal axis is a fit-pool coverage axis, not a depth axis.}}{11}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ladder}{{6}{11}{\textbf {The ladder at $\Kstar $, one panel per rival set, 3 seeds; every panel title prints the rivals' fit pool and optimiser steps.} Distinct valid novel tuples per corner against $n$: the store beside (a)~the read-path-matched rivals fitted on the 32,256-row combination-split pool for 5,040 steps, (b)~the data-matched MLP fitted for 2,560 steps on the same 32,768 rows of each rung's pool as the store's content, and (c)~the four data-matched rivals fitted on each rung's own 131,072-row pool, the store's exact rows, at 20,480 steps, or at 204,800 where the 20,480-step fit had not converged (filled dots), with the table floor in every panel (Table~\ref {tab:ladder}). Open markers are the seeds; the line is their mean. The store's margin over the strongest rival is smallest against (c) on every rung, and the store stays above every drawn rival on every rung and seed. For $n\ge 3$ the rungs probe the identical 120 corners, so the horizontal axis is a fit-pool coverage axis, not a depth axis}{figure.6}{}}
