\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The rivals were short of optimiser steps, not of data (rows 3--4, TEST, 109 corners, 3 seeds).} (a)~The MLP rival at every fit pool and step budget that was run. At 20,480 steps it scores within one tuple per corner of itself on 16,384, 32,768 and 131,072 rows, while the draft's comparator (16,384 rows, 1,280 steps) and the data-matched MLP (32,768 rows, 2,560 steps) sit near the table floor; ten and thirty times the steps on 131,072 rows add under two tuples per corner. (b)~All four families: 1,280 steps on 16,384 rows (dotted, because it is another pool), then 20,480, 204,800 and, for the MLP and the continuous MLP, 614,400 steps on the store's 131,072 rows. The blue line is the store at $\ensuremath  {K^{\star }}=32$ on 131,072 rows; the band spans its fits on 16,384, 32,768 and 131,072 rows (47.28, 47.83 and 48.01). Large markers are seed means; small open markers are the seeds.}}{12}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:headline-steps}{{7}{12}{\textbf {The rivals were short of optimiser steps, not of data (rows 3--4, TEST, 109 corners, 3 seeds).} (a)~The MLP rival at every fit pool and step budget that was run. At 20,480 steps it scores within one tuple per corner of itself on 16,384, 32,768 and 131,072 rows, while the draft's comparator (16,384 rows, 1,280 steps) and the data-matched MLP (32,768 rows, 2,560 steps) sit near the table floor; ten and thirty times the steps on 131,072 rows add under two tuples per corner. (b)~All four families: 1,280 steps on 16,384 rows (dotted, because it is another pool), then 20,480, 204,800 and, for the MLP and the continuous MLP, 614,400 steps on the store's 131,072 rows. The blue line is the store at $\Kstar =32$ on 131,072 rows; the band spans its fits on 16,384, 32,768 and 131,072 rows (47.28, 47.83 and 48.01). Large markers are seed means; small open markers are the seeds}{figure.7}{}}
