\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Deletion on the single design at $\ensuremath  {K^{\star }}$, the four measurements, rows 3--4, TEST, fit pool 131,072 rows, seeds 0, 1 and 2.} Forgetting a value or a conjunction downdates the store, downdates the address book's statistic and refits the book from it, and punches the hole; unlike the (d) rows of Table~\ref {tab:del}, which carry the book across the basis change, the book here is refit. (a)~The store against the store refit without the rows (largest mode deviation) and (b)~the refit book against the book refit without the rows (relative deviation of the rendered features; the book's count and first-moment statistic deviate by exactly 0), per scope and seed. (c)~Refusal through the hole: a display, never a result. (d)~Composition on the surviving corners before and after, and (e)~the same as a paired change with its 95\% bootstrap interval. The value deletion moves the store by under one tuple per corner; the red $\wedge $ sphere deletion lowers it by 6.13, 6.43 and 6.30 on seeds 0, 1 and 2; deleting a random 1\% of items, the control for refit instability, moves it by 0.02, 0.11 and 0.01. The conjunction loss is the deleted content, not the refit. (f)~The store after deletion minus each rival retrained without the same rows of the same pool, with 95\% intervals; on red $\wedge $ sphere the interval crosses zero against the MLP at seeds 1 and 2 and against the LSTM at seed 2.}}{29}{figure.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:deletion}{{9}{29}{\textbf {Deletion on the single design at $\Kstar $, the four measurements, rows 3--4, TEST, fit pool 131,072 rows, seeds 0, 1 and 2.} Forgetting a value or a conjunction downdates the store, downdates the address book's statistic and refits the book from it, and punches the hole; unlike the (d) rows of Table~\ref {tab:del}, which carry the book across the basis change, the book here is refit. (a)~The store against the store refit without the rows (largest mode deviation) and (b)~the refit book against the book refit without the rows (relative deviation of the rendered features; the book's count and first-moment statistic deviate by exactly 0), per scope and seed. (c)~Refusal through the hole: a display, never a result. (d)~Composition on the surviving corners before and after, and (e)~the same as a paired change with its 95\% bootstrap interval. The value deletion moves the store by under one tuple per corner; the red $\wedge $ sphere deletion lowers it by 6.13, 6.43 and 6.30 on seeds 0, 1 and 2; deleting a random 1\% of items, the control for refit instability, moves it by 0.02, 0.11 and 0.01. The conjunction loss is the deleted content, not the refit. (f)~The store after deletion minus each rival retrained without the same rows of the same pool, with 95\% intervals; on red $\wedge $ sphere the interval crosses zero against the MLP at seeds 1 and 2 and against the LSTM at seed 2}{figure.9}{}}
