\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {29}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Maze world-model rows: CMAZE-T (transition generation), TEST, Config A1, 3 seeds (one pre-registered scored run per seed).} Given the grid state and an action, generate the next state; exact transition judge. The inputs are not symmetric: the store reads a \texttt  {[bias | main | pair]} word request, the learned blind arms reduced forms of it, and the rivals the observation (\S  \ref {sec:maze-wm}); the symmetric-input rows are Table~\ref {tab:cmazet-sym}, where no condition wins: a matched transformer given the store's own pair design matches or beats the store, so the pair block, not the store, carries this table's $n$-way margin, and that row is a store row only under this asymmetric input, never an unqualified win. Config A1: latent 128, $K=2$, 6 atoms, one design pinned across seeds. Rivals are matched on read floats (MLP 4,781, $+4.3\%$; LSTM 4,290, $-6.4\%$; transformer 5,129, $+11.9\%$, against the store's 4,584). Byte convention: deployed bytes $=4\times $(atom $+$ address-book floats), float32; the float64 sufficient statistic is printed beside it, never netted. The across-wells control is the deranged one. Values are mean (seed 0 / 1 / 2). This table contains no CMAZE-O, CMAZE-1, CMAZE-2 or CMAZE-2b row.}}{39}{table.29}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:cmazet}{{29}{39}{\textbf {Maze world-model rows: CMAZE-T (transition generation), TEST, Config A1, 3 seeds (one pre-registered scored run per seed).} Given the grid state and an action, generate the next state; exact transition judge. The inputs are not symmetric: the store reads a \texttt {[bias | main | pair]} word request, the learned blind arms reduced forms of it, and the rivals the observation (\S \ref {sec:maze-wm}); the symmetric-input rows are Table~\ref {tab:cmazet-sym}, where no condition wins: a matched transformer given the store's own pair design matches or beats the store, so the pair block, not the store, carries this table's $n$-way margin, and that row is a store row only under this asymmetric input, never an unqualified win. Config A1: latent 128, $K=2$, 6 atoms, one design pinned across seeds. Rivals are matched on read floats (MLP 4,781, $+4.3\%$; LSTM 4,290, $-6.4\%$; transformer 5,129, $+11.9\%$, against the store's 4,584). Byte convention: deployed bytes $=4\times $(atom $+$ address-book floats), float32; the float64 sufficient statistic is printed beside it, never netted. The across-wells control is the deranged one. Values are mean (seed 0 / 1 / 2). This table contains no CMAZE-O, CMAZE-1, CMAZE-2 or CMAZE-2b row}{table.29}{}}
\newlabel{tab:cmaze-del}{{29}{39}{\textbf {Maze world-model rows: CMAZE-T (transition generation), TEST, Config A1, 3 seeds (one pre-registered scored run per seed).} Given the grid state and an action, generate the next state; exact transition judge. The inputs are not symmetric: the store reads a \texttt {[bias | main | pair]} word request, the learned blind arms reduced forms of it, and the rivals the observation (\S \ref {sec:maze-wm}); the symmetric-input rows are Table~\ref {tab:cmazet-sym}, where no condition wins: a matched transformer given the store's own pair design matches or beats the store, so the pair block, not the store, carries this table's $n$-way margin, and that row is a store row only under this asymmetric input, never an unqualified win. Config A1: latent 128, $K=2$, 6 atoms, one design pinned across seeds. Rivals are matched on read floats (MLP 4,781, $+4.3\%$; LSTM 4,290, $-6.4\%$; transformer 5,129, $+11.9\%$, against the store's 4,584). Byte convention: deployed bytes $=4\times $(atom $+$ address-book floats), float32; the float64 sufficient statistic is printed beside it, never netted. The across-wells control is the deranged one. Values are mean (seed 0 / 1 / 2). This table contains no CMAZE-O, CMAZE-1, CMAZE-2 or CMAZE-2b row}{table.29}{}}
